1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,800
This demonstration uses the actual
local Northstar teaching application.

2
00:00:04,870 --> 00:00:10,417
Start it with Docker Compose, open the review
page, and enter the course-only training token

3
00:00:10,487 --> 00:00:11,809
from the coding guide.

4
00:00:11,879 --> 00:00:13,479
The data is synthetic.

5
00:00:13,549 --> 00:00:16,643
The routing baseline uses understandable rules.

6
00:00:16,713 --> 00:00:19,891
The application has no
customer messaging channel.

7
00:00:19,961 --> 00:00:23,545
An incorrect token produces
an unauthorized response.

8
00:00:23,615 --> 00:00:28,373
The access boundary applies before
the request reaches the routing logic.

9
00:00:28,443 --> 00:00:32,133
A ticket cannot grant permission
by including an instruction.

10
00:00:32,203 --> 00:00:35,937
This local control demonstrates
the question of authority.

11
00:00:36,007 --> 00:00:41,361
Enterprise identity and production data
approval require a separate implementation.

12
00:00:41,431 --> 00:00:45,741
With the permitted training token, this
ticket receives an access suggestion.

13
00:00:45,811 --> 00:00:51,357
The response includes a suggestion identifier,
the rule explanation, and human review

14
00:00:51,427 --> 00:00:56,355
required. The suggestion has not yet
become a recorded operating decision.

15
00:00:56,425 --> 00:00:59,945
Inspect the text and the
proposed queue before continuing.

16
00:01:00,015 --> 00:01:04,559
Here the reviewer overrides the suggestion
to manual and saves the decision.

17
00:01:04,629 --> 00:01:08,427
The record keeps the chosen queue
and the suggestion identifier.

18
00:01:08,497 --> 00:01:11,483
A second save must not create another decision.

19
00:01:11,553 --> 00:01:12,919
No message is sent.

20
00:01:12,989 --> 00:01:18,706
In a real workflow, an override can provide
learning evidence when its reason is understood.

21
00:01:18,776 --> 00:01:22,040
The metrics distinguish
suggestions from saved decisions.

22
00:01:22,110 --> 00:01:26,014
Review time says not measured,
and adoption says not established.

23
00:01:26,084 --> 00:01:28,281
Those are honest evidence boundaries.

24
00:01:28,351 --> 00:01:34,687
To evaluate the Frame Card, define a timed task
comparison and a period of eligible workflow

25
00:01:34,757 --> 00:01:39,536
use. Functional behavior and an adopted
outcome need different evidence.
